  "findings": [
    "Every captured raw QKV row exactly reconstructs its previously saved full-block convolution history, including both repeats. All30 captured tensor rows repeat bitexact.",
    "Input normalization is bitexact between the BF16 and FP8 paths for all25600 values. One CPU-predicted BF16 norm value differs in step4, but it is shared by both observed native paths and cannot explain their difference.",
    "All25600 observed FP8 activation bytes and five scales exactly match true-division per-token E4M3 quantization. All52428800 QKV weight bytes and10240 scale replicas exactly match the declared packed-tensor weight recipe. No weight export or activation quantizer defect found.",
    "The earliest additional arithmetic discrepancy is pc3 GemmFp8: exact same quantized operands versus an exact binary64 dot with nested FP32 scale epilogue differs by0.2773\u20130.6843% relL2. The CPU FP32 dot differs from that exact reference by at most0.001982% relL2 in these five rows, so CPU dot rounding does not explain the native residual.",
    "The BF16-rounded output of a fully binary64 epilogue equals the nested FP32 epilogue in all five rows. Epilogue reassociation does not explain this measured discrepancy.",
    "The observed FP8-vs-BF16 raw QKV discrepancy remains1.0837\u20131.7305%. Intended weight and activation quantization contribute; the additional native-vs-exact-quantized-dot discrepancy appears at GEMM, before recurrence. No conclusion about all subsequent recurrent/MLP errors or model output quality follows.",
    "Deployed object ab3ab392 has FAST_ACCUM=1 and accumulates across the whole K=5120 with the same WGMMA register chain. Systematic magnitude shrink is compatible with accumulation precision loss, but no controlled accumulation-policy experiment has run. A load/layout defect is not excluded solely by this source audit."
